      "satisfied": true,
      "reason": "The loader satisfies all deterministic rules. No Math.random or Date.now in core logic. No network calls. All filesystem reads are deterministic relative to filesystem state (readdir, readFile on declared paths — covered by exception 3). Directory entries are sorted via localeCompare at graph-loader.ts:126, graph-loader.ts:209, graph-loader.ts:229, graph-loader.ts:245, ensuring stable ordering across platforms. SHA-256 hashing is delegated to cli/utils (not directly called here). Token estimation is not performed in this file. No implicit system state is accessed. The fallback config (graph-loader.ts:28-31) and fallback architecture (graph-loader.ts:90-100) are constant values, not system-state-dependent. Error handling stores messages deterministically. All inputs (projectRoot, options) fully determine outputs given identical filesystem state."
    },
    "silent-missing-files": {
      "satisfied": true,
      "reason": "All three directories covered by the aspect are handled with silent fallbacks. `loadAspects` (line 194-201) wraps the entire scan in try/catch and returns `[]` on any error. `loadFlows` (line 226-241) catches on `readdir` failure at line 228-231 and returns `[]`. `loadSchemas` (line 243-257) wraps everything in try/catch and returns `[]` on failure. The drift-state store is not in this node's source file, so it is out of scope here. All three graph-loader targets named in the aspect (`aspects/`, `flows/`, `schemas/`) correctly treat missing directories as empty state rather than throwing."
    }
